WEBVTT

00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:06.560
Sure enough, the Book of God

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.440
was not meant to fall into human hands.

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:10.570
Don't tell me...

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:13.020
If the Puzzle of God is solved,

00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:14.480
this is what will happen?!

00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:19.360
What I'm seeing really is the future?

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:21.010
Is this the world that you wanted?

00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:22.730
Tell me, Jin!

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:25.780
Jin!

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:40.760
Kaito
Observation Record

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:42.950
Kaito...

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:05.870
Kimi no nounai e to shinnyuu
Gonna infiltrate your brain

00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:08.670
Nemutteru suki ni baby, open the gate
While you're sleeping, baby, open the gate

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:10.460
Fukuzatsusugi security
Too-complicated security

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:13.210
Kakusareru to abakitakunaru
When something's hidden, it makes me want to expose it

00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:17.720
Barabara ni chirabatte iru password o hiroiatsume
I'll gather up those loose, scattered passwords

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:22.430
Kakushin ni sematte yuku, sono shoutai o misete
And approach the core, so show me that true form

00:01:22.430 --> 00:01:24.640
Kantan ni clear dekinai
I can't clear it easily

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:27.310
Saki nante motto yomenai
Can read what lies ahead even less

00:01:27.310 --> 00:01:29.310
Kaidoku fukanou smile
A smile that can't be deciphered

00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:31.610
Kiken na puzzle
A dangerous puzzle

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:33.570
Lock sareteta door aru nara
If there's a door that's been locked

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:36.360
Zutto tataite miru beki, kaza-ana hiraku wa
You must keep striking it, a crack will open

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:40.910
Eien ni hodokenai nazo nanka wa nai
No mystery remains unsolved forever

00:01:40.910 --> 00:01:43.160
Makiokosu, it's a supernova!
It's forming, it's a supernova!

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:47.830
Tobikiri shigekiteki na hirameki o agemashou
I will give you thoroughly stimulating insight

00:01:47.830 --> 00:01:50.080
Misskey-misskey la-tu-ma

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:52.420
Yume no naka, it's a supernova!
In the middle of a dream, it's a supernova!

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:55.050
Watashi wa, sou, brain diver
I am, yes, a brain diver

00:01:55.050 --> 00:02:00.930
Kimi ga sagashimotometeru kotae ni nareru made
Until I become familiar with the answer you seek

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:06.600
Brain diver

00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:11.400
Brain diver

00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:19.990
Glistening Tears

00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:54.860
It would seem this stores
something most important.

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:05.220
I'd heard there was

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:08.200
a new Giver who
had defeated Kaito Daimon.

00:03:08.590 --> 00:03:12.340
Well done, Galileo, aka Gammon.

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:13.290
The principal!

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:15.380
Your ass is still alive?!

00:03:15.770 --> 00:03:17.350
Yes...

00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:20.900
But as you can see, I've been captured.

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:22.100
Huh?!

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:24.140
But you're just walkin' around!

00:03:25.550 --> 00:03:30.250
Walking around is one thing,
but escape is impossible.

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:36.100
Did you get that problem earlier?

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:36.960
I couldn't solve it at all!

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:38.570
I know, right?

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:39.830
Can't be helped, huh?

00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:48.120
Dammit!

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:49.380
Quit followin' me!

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:51.300
What happened to you last night?

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:53.310
You just suddenly disappeared!

00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:55.270
I was worried about you!

00:03:55.270 --> 00:03:58.010
That's got nothin' to do with someone
who can't solve puzzles!

00:03:58.010 --> 00:04:01.350
I..I can, just you watch.

00:04:05.630 --> 00:04:07.050
I don't get it!

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:08.840
What's going on?

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:11.360
Fine, I'll tell you:

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:15.080
I have to take on a Puzzle of Fools!

00:04:15.830 --> 00:04:17.520
You're just in the way.

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:19.080
That's not it.

00:04:19.080 --> 00:04:21.010
You're hiding something!

00:04:21.330 --> 00:04:22.860
I can feel it!

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:24.320
Huh?

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:25.740
"Something," you say?!

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:36.670
Hey! Explain yourself, Kaito!

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:43.520
What the...

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:45.070
Nonoha!

00:04:45.070 --> 00:04:46.340
Where'd you go?

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:47.400
Nonoha!

00:04:53.670 --> 00:04:54.730
Kaito?

00:04:55.340 --> 00:04:56.350
Kaito?

00:04:56.690 --> 00:04:57.440
Kaito!

00:05:00.340 --> 00:05:01.450
What's wrong with you?

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:03.190
You didn't hear me calling?

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:06.240
H..H..Hey!

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:10.760
Ka..Ka..Kaito?

00:05:11.470 --> 00:05:12.620
Thank goodness.

00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:15.000
Kaito?

00:05:15.490 --> 00:05:16.470
Please.

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:18.000
I mean it, please.

00:05:18.570 --> 00:05:20.090
Stay away from me.

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:24.260
Ka..Kaito?

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:26.090
Please wait.

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:30.050
I have something important to tell you.

00:05:34.890 --> 00:05:37.190
It's been a while, Kaito.

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:40.100
Cubik, what's going on?

00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:42.300
What's this "something
important" you mentioned?

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:46.300
This is...

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:49.870
I've been observing you this whole time.

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:51.450
"Observing" me?

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:52.490
Now look here!

00:05:53.110 --> 00:05:55.820
This data displays your brain's ability

00:05:55.820 --> 00:05:58.540
to decipher puzzle-related information.

00:05:58.870 --> 00:06:01.590
Put simply, this is your thinking speed.

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:03.100
Thinking speed?

00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:03.670
Yes...

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:07.600
This line represents the
theoretical human boundary.

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:09.640
Huh? So that means...

00:06:10.060 --> 00:06:13.230
Kaito has accelerated, tremendously.

00:06:13.710 --> 00:06:16.020
Such that he's exceeded human boundaries.

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:17.030
Huh?

00:06:17.680 --> 00:06:20.760
Kaito, have you become unable to
see things on your periphery,

00:06:20.760 --> 00:06:23.270
or become deaf to certain sounds?

00:06:24.990 --> 00:06:26.190
You have, haven't you?

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:29.290
To speed up, to cross that boundary,

00:06:29.290 --> 00:06:31.830
your brain has been shutting
out other information.

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:37.620
And? What does that mean?

00:06:37.970 --> 00:06:39.260
At this rate,

00:06:39.260 --> 00:06:42.720
your thinking speed
will reach impossible levels.

00:06:42.720 --> 00:06:43.880
When that happens...

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:45.000
What is it?

00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:47.250
I don't know.

00:06:47.250 --> 00:06:50.370
Something unthinkable may happen.

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:51.720
For example...

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:53.140
For example?

00:06:53.670 --> 00:06:56.880
No, I don't think it's possible, but...

00:06:57.590 --> 00:07:00.750
Still, I can't tell
just what might happen.

00:07:01.460 --> 00:07:03.480
Just one thing is certain.

00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:07.220
If he continues to cross
the limit like this,

00:07:07.220 --> 00:07:08.650
at some point...

00:07:13.060 --> 00:07:15.960
The acceleration is
especially fierce when

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:17.820
the Armlet of Orpheus is active.

00:07:18.780 --> 00:07:19.960
Kaito!

00:07:20.280 --> 00:07:22.990
You'd be better off not
solving puzzles anymore.

00:07:22.990 --> 00:07:24.630
You'll cease to be yourself.

00:07:24.860 --> 00:07:26.250
Before that happens...

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:33.970
Mind your own business.

00:07:35.840 --> 00:07:36.530
Kaito?

00:07:36.530 --> 00:07:37.310
Kaito!

00:07:38.010 --> 00:07:39.810
Hey, Kaito!

00:07:43.330 --> 00:07:45.580
Hang on a minute, Kaito!

00:07:45.580 --> 00:07:47.760
So you buy that story?

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:51.140
Well, you've been weird recently!

00:07:51.140 --> 00:07:52.700
Even earlier, you were...

00:07:52.980 --> 00:07:54.930
I will solve puzzles.

00:07:54.930 --> 00:07:56.200
No matter what!

00:07:56.660 --> 00:07:57.870
But why?!

00:07:57.870 --> 00:08:01.000
Why not just ignore Rook and Gammon?

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:03.170
You want to get back at
whoever killed your parents?

00:08:04.280 --> 00:08:06.530
You want to help this "Jin" person?

00:08:06.530 --> 00:08:08.340
Hey, Kaito!

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:11.670
No one's happy about the bad things

00:08:11.670 --> 00:08:12.880
that have happened to you!

00:08:19.220 --> 00:08:20.350
Nonoha!

00:08:23.220 --> 00:08:24.600
Thanks for all you've done for me.

00:08:29.090 --> 00:08:30.760
He's gone, huh?

00:08:31.690 --> 00:08:34.260
No one can stop Kaito.

00:08:35.300 --> 00:08:37.450
I knew that from the start.

00:08:39.430 --> 00:08:41.660
There's something I want
you to help me with.

00:08:43.790 --> 00:08:45.460
We've been waiting for you,

00:08:45.890 --> 00:08:48.840
Einstein, Kaito Daimon.

00:09:03.160 --> 00:09:05.460
I can't say that a Puzzle
of Fools of this caliber

00:09:05.460 --> 00:09:08.470
would assist Kaito Daimon's development.

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:10.900
Why use something like this now?

00:09:12.260 --> 00:09:13.900
I want to make certain.

00:09:14.420 --> 00:09:17.070
Does this have something to do with his

00:09:17.070 --> 00:09:19.020
having lost to Gammon Sakanoue?

00:09:19.930 --> 00:09:22.560
Kaito may have entered the final

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:25.000
phase of achieving Phi-Brain status.

00:09:25.570 --> 00:09:29.590
He may be shutting all out
to concentrate on solving puzzles.

00:09:30.360 --> 00:09:31.880
"Shutting all out"?

00:09:32.520 --> 00:09:35.290
At last, you've reached this point.

00:09:36.980 --> 00:09:38.890
Do you not think it strange?

00:09:38.890 --> 00:09:39.970
Huh?

00:09:40.360 --> 00:09:42.660
Our director, Rook.

00:09:47.540 --> 00:09:48.440
This is...

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:52.150
The portal to the POG
headquarters' central system.

00:09:52.330 --> 00:09:54.890
You've been hacking into it?

00:09:54.890 --> 00:09:56.250
But that's...

00:09:56.250 --> 00:09:57.970
I don't believe it!

00:10:10.370 --> 00:10:14.080
Cubik, just what are you doing?

00:10:14.570 --> 00:10:16.840
Rook Banjo Crossfield...

00:10:17.310 --> 00:10:20.140
He's trying to mold
Kaito into a Phi-Brain.

00:10:21.110 --> 00:10:23.520
By order of Count Pythagoras.

00:10:23.970 --> 00:10:25.940
Is that really so?

00:10:27.620 --> 00:10:31.690
I can't help but think there's
something else to this.

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:35.860
Do you not think that someone
possessing such capabilities

00:10:35.860 --> 00:10:39.700
is more suited to be
Kaito Daimon's companion?

00:10:44.660 --> 00:10:45.540
Kaito...

00:10:52.720 --> 00:10:54.180
Rook's goal?

00:10:54.740 --> 00:10:59.220
Is all this due to Count
Pythagoras's orders?

00:11:00.230 --> 00:11:02.680
I feel that something is being hidden.

00:11:02.680 --> 00:11:04.240
Hey, there!

00:11:04.240 --> 00:11:06.810
I'm a POG Giver now.

00:11:08.070 --> 00:11:09.330
Indeed.

00:11:09.900 --> 00:11:12.810
Still, you've certainly thrown caution
to the wind, haven't you?

00:11:12.810 --> 00:11:14.170
Yeah!

00:11:14.170 --> 00:11:15.900
I'm gonna solve the Puzzle of God.

00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:18.490
You may well lose your life.

00:11:18.840 --> 00:11:20.720
Looks who's talkin', bastard.

00:11:20.720 --> 00:11:23.240
If you go around puttin' on airs,

00:11:23.240 --> 00:11:24.490
you're gonna get hurt.

00:11:33.770 --> 00:11:36.250
But I can't go any further.

00:11:36.790 --> 00:11:38.630
Even the computer's analysis says

00:11:38.630 --> 00:11:40.920
this should be the answer.

00:11:40.920 --> 00:11:42.180
But...

00:11:50.010 --> 00:11:51.230
Cubik?

00:11:51.630 --> 00:11:54.350
Please, Upperclassman Jikukawa!

00:11:54.350 --> 00:11:56.230
Please lend me your help!

00:11:56.750 --> 00:11:59.920
I know that you're a POG, too.

00:12:00.660 --> 00:12:02.870
If this were leaked to the POG...

00:12:03.530 --> 00:12:04.510
But!

00:12:12.170 --> 00:12:14.170
Did you prepare everything yourself?

00:12:14.170 --> 00:12:17.990
This is the only thing I can do.

00:12:19.240 --> 00:12:21.130
Knowing Kaito's past, I...

00:12:21.130 --> 00:12:24.510
I thought I could help him somehow.

00:12:26.740 --> 00:12:28.850
Numbers were my only friend.

00:12:29.550 --> 00:12:31.630
Only my computers, and Okabe.

00:12:32.360 --> 00:12:34.720
I thought that was enough!

00:12:34.720 --> 00:12:37.320
But I want to be friends.

00:12:38.060 --> 00:12:40.150
I want to be friends with Kaito.

00:12:40.610 --> 00:12:44.040
Maybe I don't have the right
to think that way, but...

00:12:45.960 --> 00:12:49.050
Oh, jeez, haven't you noticed?

00:12:50.390 --> 00:12:54.390
You've been Kaito's friend
for a long, long time.

00:13:04.740 --> 00:13:06.510
But I'm a Giver.

00:13:06.990 --> 00:13:10.010
Unfortunately, solving
puzzles isn't my forte.

00:13:10.010 --> 00:13:11.100
Oh, no!

00:13:11.580 --> 00:13:16.400
Still, the truth is, I originally
wanted to be Solver.

00:13:20.280 --> 00:13:23.990
I believed in the POG, in
a sacred commandment...

00:13:23.990 --> 00:13:25.990
to seal prizes,

00:13:25.990 --> 00:13:29.250
people's feelings inside
of puzzles, and to protect them.

00:13:29.920 --> 00:13:31.410
I want to know, too.

00:13:32.040 --> 00:13:35.370
Just what is happening to the POG now?

00:13:40.860 --> 00:13:41.850
Please.

00:13:42.400 --> 00:13:43.420
I mean it, please.

00:13:43.850 --> 00:13:45.510
Stay away from me.

00:13:46.600 --> 00:13:48.010
Thanks for all you've done for me.

00:13:48.860 --> 00:13:50.000
Kaito...

00:13:52.240 --> 00:13:54.880
I can't get past this screen.

00:13:55.330 --> 00:13:57.520
I've tried different things, but...

00:13:57.520 --> 00:13:58.910
It's the golden ratio.

00:13:58.910 --> 00:13:59.560
Huh?

00:14:00.040 --> 00:14:02.150
This is the Greek letter "phi."

00:14:02.150 --> 00:14:03.420
Oh!

00:14:03.420 --> 00:14:07.140
Phi can be used as a symbol to
represent the golden ratio!

00:14:07.910 --> 00:14:11.740
All members of the POG have
this number memorized.

00:14:11.740 --> 00:14:14.760
To those who seek the perfect puzzle,

00:14:14.760 --> 00:14:17.200
phi is the most beautiful of numbers.

00:14:17.600 --> 00:14:19.270
The golden ratio.

00:14:22.400 --> 00:14:23.460
Dual surfaces?

00:14:24.720 --> 00:14:27.900
Each tile has a figure drawn on the rear.

00:14:27.900 --> 00:14:31.050
We have to get both sides
right to solve the puzzle!

00:14:31.050 --> 00:14:32.640
No way!

00:14:32.640 --> 00:14:35.060
If we have to solve
each individual piece,

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:36.680
it will take forever!

00:14:37.330 --> 00:14:40.480
Sure enough, this is a hard one.

00:14:40.810 --> 00:14:42.830
Lining up both sides...

00:14:42.830 --> 00:14:44.730
That won't be easy to compute!

00:14:45.130 --> 00:14:46.560
Don't go giving up like that!

00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:48.650
There are two of us.

00:14:49.140 --> 00:14:51.320
We'll work together.

00:15:01.450 --> 00:15:05.030
There is a puzzle hidden
inside this structure.

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:08.970
Please find and solve it
within the allotted time.

00:15:09.420 --> 00:15:11.950
And? What kind of puzzle is it?

00:15:11.950 --> 00:15:13.510
I cannot tell you.

00:15:13.510 --> 00:15:14.810
What?!

00:15:14.810 --> 00:15:17.610
That, too, is one of the rules.

00:15:18.270 --> 00:15:20.140
You will have ten minutes.

00:15:20.720 --> 00:15:23.210
If you do not solve it within this time,

00:15:23.210 --> 00:15:25.670
you will fall into the
pulverizer behind you.

00:15:27.570 --> 00:15:28.900
Now then....

00:15:28.900 --> 00:15:31.910
Puzzle time, let's start.

00:15:42.510 --> 00:15:44.960
So there's a puzzle hidden
somewhere inside all this?

00:16:01.420 --> 00:16:03.390
Is that it, Rook?

00:16:03.390 --> 00:16:05.020
That's what this is?!

00:16:08.310 --> 00:16:10.790
I'm going to try moving
this to the right.

00:16:11.210 --> 00:16:12.180
Okay.

00:16:14.760 --> 00:16:16.640
Kaito's sensor is going off!

00:16:17.280 --> 00:16:19.250
Kaito is solving a puzzle.

00:16:19.880 --> 00:16:21.050
What was that?

00:16:21.050 --> 00:16:22.220
We have to stop him!

00:16:22.220 --> 00:16:23.830
Keep working.

00:16:24.630 --> 00:16:25.540
It's all right.

00:16:25.790 --> 00:16:27.280
I'm on it.

00:16:31.400 --> 00:16:34.530
Kaito has begun to awaken
to his Phi-Brain potential.

00:16:34.990 --> 00:16:36.500
He's shutting out information,

00:16:36.500 --> 00:16:39.830
his thoughts breaking past
limits and growing faster...

00:16:39.830 --> 00:16:41.560
Just what lies ahead of him?

00:16:41.560 --> 00:16:45.600
Maybe he will become
able to see the future.

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:46.940
The future?

00:16:47.240 --> 00:16:51.890
Using shards of information,
predict what could occur

00:16:51.890 --> 00:16:54.020
and see them as visions...

00:16:54.670 --> 00:16:55.970
I don't know.

00:16:55.970 --> 00:16:58.700
This is nothing more than conjecture.

00:17:00.870 --> 00:17:02.450
Wait!

00:17:02.450 --> 00:17:03.970
I ain't waitin'!

00:17:03.970 --> 00:17:05.310
Aw, c'mon!

00:17:06.560 --> 00:17:08.120
Hey, Kaito!

00:17:09.710 --> 00:17:12.700
Here, I made these for you.

00:17:12.700 --> 00:17:14.260
Eat them and feel better.

00:17:24.550 --> 00:17:25.930
That's disgusting!

00:17:25.930 --> 00:17:27.650
Who could eat somethin' like this?!

00:17:28.100 --> 00:17:29.890
I'm gonna die!

00:17:29.890 --> 00:17:32.280
Hey, that's really rude!

00:17:32.690 --> 00:17:33.750
I swear!

00:17:47.400 --> 00:17:48.400
What's this?

00:17:55.100 --> 00:17:59.470
Now then, show me your
skill, Kaito Daimon.

00:18:24.880 --> 00:18:25.980
It's a code.

00:18:26.360 --> 00:18:29.670
The sound and light
combine to form letters.

00:18:37.320 --> 00:18:38.960
Devices fixed at each of the

00:18:38.960 --> 00:18:40.660
eight gates emit light and sound.

00:18:41.160 --> 00:18:43.240
Seven sounds, from DO to TI,

00:18:43.240 --> 00:18:44.540
and four colors of light,

00:18:44.540 --> 00:18:46.270
corresponding to four rows and seven

00:18:46.270 --> 00:18:47.270
columns of Roman numerals.

00:18:50.700 --> 00:18:51.860
The answer is...

00:18:52.280 --> 00:18:53.610
Phi-Brain!

00:18:59.870 --> 00:19:01.990
Impossible! Such speed!

00:19:02.440 --> 00:19:04.060
He's already solved it?!

00:19:23.080 --> 00:19:25.620
Hey, ain't someone there?

00:19:25.620 --> 00:19:26.220
Hey!

00:19:27.130 --> 00:19:28.180
Kaito!

00:19:28.450 --> 00:19:29.920
Calm down.
Hey!

00:19:29.920 --> 00:19:31.560
It's all right, Kaito.

00:19:32.490 --> 00:19:33.280
Kaito!

00:19:34.950 --> 00:19:36.820
What's going on? What's going on?!

00:19:37.330 --> 00:19:38.190
Stop it!

00:19:38.640 --> 00:19:39.930
I get it!

00:19:40.200 --> 00:19:43.120
You don't want to involve us in this.

00:19:43.120 --> 00:19:45.080
You're trying to do it on your own.

00:19:45.400 --> 00:19:46.670
But!

00:19:48.330 --> 00:19:50.590
I can't do that.

00:19:50.590 --> 00:19:53.530
I can't have you sad, or suffering.

00:19:54.320 --> 00:19:57.840
If you can keep your
head up, then so can I.

00:19:58.760 --> 00:20:00.330
Why do you think that is?

00:20:01.320 --> 00:20:02.470
It's strange, isn't it?

00:20:13.180 --> 00:20:16.160
I want you to feel better.

00:20:16.900 --> 00:20:18.860
I'll make you feel better.

00:20:19.660 --> 00:20:20.990
So...

00:20:21.600 --> 00:20:24.490
Please, let me be by your side.

00:20:59.480 --> 00:21:00.690
We've solved it!

00:21:35.540 --> 00:21:36.940
That was well played.

00:21:36.940 --> 00:21:39.880
All right, I'll go with castling.

00:21:44.800 --> 00:21:47.800
Ah, you certainly are incredible!

00:21:49.480 --> 00:21:52.230
I made certain of it today.

00:21:52.920 --> 00:21:54.560
There's no mistake:

00:21:54.560 --> 00:21:56.870
Kaito has begun to awaken.

00:21:59.350 --> 00:22:00.690
Kaito...

00:22:00.690 --> 00:22:03.230
That's right, Jin.

00:22:08.440 --> 00:22:10.050
He will be here soon...

00:22:18.300 --> 00:22:20.140
To the world of the Phi-Brain.

00:22:37.240 --> 00:22:41.540
Tsukue no ue de umareta sekai
A world born on top of a desk

00:22:41.540 --> 00:22:47.340
Ichiban saki ni kimi ni misetakatta
I wanted to show it to you first of all

00:22:47.770 --> 00:22:52.090
Karappo no heya sotto nukedashite
I sneaked silently out of that empty room

00:22:52.090 --> 00:22:57.210
Hashirihajimeteta
And started running

00:22:58.290 --> 00:23:02.610
Iki hazumasete oka o noboru to
Breathing heavily, I climbed the hill

00:23:02.610 --> 00:23:08.220
Kimi ga saki ni tsuite matte ita ne
And you were already there, waiting

00:23:08.900 --> 00:23:13.160
Takusan no hajimete kimi to mitsuketa
There were so many treasures that I first

00:23:13.160 --> 00:23:17.910
Takaramono datta
Discovered with you

00:23:18.410 --> 00:23:24.020
Kanashisa de afureta toki wa
That time when I was overcome with sadness

00:23:24.020 --> 00:23:26.600
Nanimo iwazu ni tada
You said nothing

00:23:26.600 --> 00:23:29.250
Soba ni ite kureta ne
Just stayed there by my side, didn't you?

00:23:29.250 --> 00:23:33.910
Imademo wasurenai yo
Even now, I haven't forgotten

00:23:33.910 --> 00:23:39.180
Mata aou ne, yakusoku o shiyou
Let's meet again, let's make it a promise

00:23:39.180 --> 00:23:44.400
Kei wa shinai, ano hi no sayonara
It won't fade, the "goodbye" of that day

00:23:44.400 --> 00:23:50.050
Boku no subete, kimi ga kureta michi
Everything I have, the path you gave me

00:23:50.050 --> 00:23:58.960
Zutto kokoro no naka hikaru yo
Will always shine within my heart

00:24:03.600 --> 00:24:05.500
It seems that, at last, the time has come

00:24:05.500 --> 00:24:06.900
to share the secrets
regarding myself and Jin.

00:24:06.900 --> 00:24:09.010
I ain't interested in
your old-ass stories.

00:24:09.010 --> 00:24:11.470
We were there alongside the POG.

00:24:11.470 --> 00:24:14.060
I should be able to help
solve your mystery.

00:24:14.060 --> 00:24:16.140
Fine, I guess it can't
be helped. Start talkin'!

00:24:16.140 --> 00:24:18.190
Well, where should I begin?

00:24:18.190 --> 00:24:19.710
Chapter 1, "My First Warm Bath,"

00:24:19.710 --> 00:24:21.830
Chapter 2, "A Tearful
Farewell to the Breast"?

00:24:21.830 --> 00:24:23.770
Next time, "That Which
Inherits Principles"

00:24:22.500 --> 00:24:27.500
That Which Inherits Principles

00:24:23.770 --> 00:24:26.730
Or Chapter 48, "My Third
Farewell to the Breast"?
